Managers and Leaders (including laboratory supervisors)
(7)
Managers and leaders, including laboratory supervisors are responsible for ensuring:
Regulated chemicals are identified and documented within their areas of responsibility;
Risk assessment processes are undertaken and risk controls are rigorously followed;
An adequate level of training and induction is undertaken and recorded;
Permit or licensing requirements are sought, where required;
Local area emergency processes are developed, exercised and periodically reviewed; and
The periodic (assurance) review of chemical management documentation.

Health and Safety Team
(8)
The Health and Safety are responsible for:
Providing oversight and monitoring this Procedure;
Providing advice on hazards and risks to consider;
Providing advice on risk control measures and emergency preparedness;
Providing advice and oversight with permit / licensing requirements;
Supporting assurance processes; and
Supporting incident response, investigation and sharing the lessons learnt across the organisation.
